<title>USA: Fleet weighs buying brokerage business.</title>
<headline>Fleet weighs buying brokerage business.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mark Wheeler, senior executive vice president at Fleet Bank, said Tuesday the bank was weighing whether to move into the brokerage business.</p>
<p>&quot;We've looked at brokerage operations,&quot; he said. &quot;Really, it is extremely appealing.&quot;</p>
<p>Wheeler spoke at a business breakfast sponsored by Crain's New York Business. He declined to elaborate.</p>
<p>Broker Advest Group Inc rose sharply last week on takeover speculation, with Fleet one of the rumored suitors.</p>
</text>
